### Describe the Bug

Client side values are rejected on update for:
- `tfa_secret` (unconditionally)
- `provider` (authenticated non-admin)
- `external_identifier` (authenticated non-admin)

https://github.com/directus/directus/blob/a5da59da94bb33c8d644df93a21403eca4c1a4e7/api/src/services/users.ts#L308-L328

`createOne` and `createMany` aren't guarded which means that a `tfa_secret` written through the create path bypasses verification on `TFAService.enableTFA`:
https://github.com/directus/directus/blob/a5da59da94bb33c8d644df93a21403eca4c1a4e7/api/src/services/tfa.ts#L64-L82

SSO drivers rely on the ability to `createOne` with `provider` and `external_identifier` so the fix should mirror update and:

| field | reject on create when |
| --- | --- |
| `tfa_secret` | always |
| `provider`, `external_identifier` | `accountability && !accountability.admin` |

#### Related

#28142 - calls out a similar problem for `tfa_secret` but it's a different place


### To Reproduce

```bash
# appropriately rejected - "You can't change the "tfa_secret" value manually"
curl -X PATCH "localhost:8055/users/<id> -H "Authorization: Bearer <admin-token>" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"tfa_secret": "H4CK3D"}'

# accepted
curl -X POST "localhost:8055/users" -H "Authorization: Bearer <admin-token>" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"email":"v@example.com","password":"hunter2","tfa_secret":"H4CK3D"}'
```

The exposure is higher if a non-admin is granted `create` to `directus_users`

The fix should pass:
```ts
// inserted into /api/src/services/users.test.ts at
// describe('restricted auth fields', () => { 
			describe('should disallow creation for non-admin users', () => {
				const service = new UsersService({
					knex: db,
					schema,
					accountability: { role: 'test', admin: false } as Accountability,
				});

				it.each(['tfa_secret', 'provider', 'external_identifier'])('%s', async (field) => {
					const opts: MutationOptions = {};

					await service.createOne({ [field]: 'test' }, opts);

					expect(superCreateOneSpy).toHaveBeenCalled();

					expect(opts.preMutationError).toStrictEqual(
						new InvalidPayloadError({ reason: `You can't change the "${field}" value manually` }),
					);
				});
			});

			describe.each([
				['admin users', { role: 'admin', admin: true } as Accountability],
				['null accountability', null],
			])('should allow creation for %s', (_, accountability) => {
				const service = new UsersService({
					knex: db,
					schema,
					accountability,
				});

				it.each(['provider', 'external_identifier'])('%s', async (field) => {
					const promise = service.createOne({ [field]: 'test' });

					await expect(promise).resolves.not.toThrow();

					expect(superCreateOneSpy.mock.lastCall![0]).toEqual(expect.objectContaining({ [field]: 'test' }));
				});
			});

```

