### Describe the Bug

This could be listed as three independend bugs, but I think they are all symptoms for the client-side permission evaluation in the insights module needing maintenance.
As far as I can tell, executing actions that falsely appear to be available in the user interface will ultimately result in an error message, but it's still unnecessarily confusing for end users, also it looks rather broken.

Custom permissions are not evaluated correctly for A) the dashboard overview, where edit / delete options are available for all dashboards as soon as the current user has the respective permission for _any_ dashboard:

https://github.com/directus/directus/blob/c76747d8d28970fbbe4d4ff7de85b2e0fcb6f716/app/src/modules/insights/routes/overview.vue#L48

and B) the insights dashboard edit mode; the permission is queried for `directus_panels` with the current `directus_dashboard`'s primary key:

https://github.com/directus/directus/blob/c76747d8d28970fbbe4d4ff7de85b2e0fcb6f716/app/src/modules/insights/routes/dashboard.vue#L50

The B behaviour can be mitigated with this super dirty workaround:
```
import { defineHook } from '@directus/extensions-sdk';

export default defineHook(({ init }) => {
  init('routes.before', (meta) => {
    meta.app.get('/permissions/me/:collection/:pk?', (req, res, next) => {
      const { collection, pk } = req.params;
      if (collection === 'directus_panels') {
        return res.redirect(`/permissions/me/directus_dashboards/${pk}`);
      }
      return next();
    });
  });
});

```

Once the workaround is in place, the 3rd partial bug can be reproduced: When switching boards via the module navigation, the edit button's state is not updated. Refreshing or directly opening the dashboard will yield the correct disabled state, but it will be retained without recheck for other dashboards opened via module links.


I'm not using the latest version of Directus, but since the code seems to still be unchanged on main, I'd expect this to be reproducible nevertheless.

### To Reproduce

1. have at least 2 insights dashboards
2. create a custom policy granting read access for all insights content and full access for a specific dashboard, e.g.
    - `directus_dashboards`.read: full access
    - `directus_dashboards`.update: set item permission rule to `{"_and":[{"id":{"_eq":"<DASHBOARD_ID>"}}]}` and select all fields
    - `directus_dashboards`.delete: set item permission rule to `{"_and":[{"id":{"_eq":"<DASHBOARD_ID>"}}]}`
    - `directus_panels`.create: full access
    - `directus_panels`.read: full access
    - `directus_panels`.update: set item permission rule to `{"_and":[{"dashboard":{"id":{"_eq":"<DASHBOARD_ID>"}}}]}` and select all fields
    - `directus_panels`.delete: set item permission rule to `{"_and":[{"dashboard":{"id":{"_eq":"<DASHBOARD_ID>"}}}]}`
3. assign custom policy to non-admin user (ensure no conflicting insights policies exist)
4. open /admin/insights with user updated in previous step
    - all dashboards are visible (as expected)
    - edit / delete buttons are available for _all_ ❌ dashboards and will trigger forbidden error messages when executed for a dashboard the current user has no respective permissions for
6. open /admin/insights/<DASHBOARD_ID> -> edit button is disabled ❌
7. change custom policy to grant full access for `directus_panels`.update 
    - now editation mode can be entered for all dashboards

