### Describe the Bug

When referencing fields of a may to many relation in a collections permissions while wrongly specifying the name of the foreign key the behavior during update attempts differs depending on the underlying database.

In my example there are two collections (`rockets` and `missions`) and the junction table ` rockets_missions`. The correct foreign key in the junction table is called `rockets_id`. I specified update permissions on the junction table in to different incorrect ways and tested the behavior using MariaDB and PostgresSQL.

Correct Permission:
```
{
  "_and": [
    {
      "rockets_id":
        {
          "id" : { "_eq": "1" }
        }
    }
  ]
}
```

Permission1 (invalid foreign key):
```
{
  "_and": [
    {
      "rocket_id":
        {
          "id" : { "_eq": "1" }
        }
    }
  ]
}
```

Permission 2 (invalid foreign table column):
```
{
  "_and": [
    {
      "rockets_id":
        {
          "ids" : { "_eq": "1" }
        }
    }
  ]
}
```

| Database | Permission1 | Permission2 |
|--------|--------|--------|
| PostgresSQL | 500 - Error 1 | 500 - Error 2 |
| MariaDB | 204 - Success | 500 - Error 2 |

Error 1:
```
ERROR: select (CASE WHEN 1 THEN 1 END) AS "missions_id", 1 as "id" from "rockets_missions" where ("rockets_missions"."id" in ($1)) limit $2 - argument of CASE/WHEN must be type boolean, not type integer
```

Error 2:
```
ERROR: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'type')
```

While I think the second case is OK as it is I see two issues with the first one:

1. Using MariaDB (and probably every driver except Postgres) this permission results in "always true" which I think can be problematic
2. The Postgres error occurs because the fallback value in the [case when builder](https://github.com/directus/directus/blob/b6bbc3b138f3d4dbde44dc4045efc4e6e9f9ed56/api/src/database/run-ast/utils/apply-case-when.ts#L48) is set to 1 which is not a valid boolean value in PostgresSQL. The addition of the fallback let's me believe that there is a scenario in which it is used without having configuration errors. However I was unable to find it. In this case the exception would be more problematic.

I am willing to provide a PR to fix this. However I will need feedback on what the desired behavior in this case is.

