Many component tests repeat the same setup patterns:

- DOM outlet creation (menu-outlet, dialog-outlet) — found in many test files
- Global mount config (i18n, pinia, directives)
- Directive mocks (ClickOutside, Md, Tooltip) — repeated imports across many tests

### Current

Each test file manually sets up:

```ts
const global = {
  plugins: [i18n, createTestingPinia({ createSpy: vi.fn })],
  directives: {
    'click-outside': ClickOutside,
    md: Md,
    tooltip: Tooltip,
  },
};

beforeEach(() => {
  for (const id of ['menu-outlet', 'dialog-outlet']) {
    if (!document.getElementById(id)) {
      const el = document.createElement('div');
      el.id = id;
      document.body.appendChild(el);
    }
  }
});

afterEach(() => {
  for (const id of ['menu-outlet', 'dialog-outlet']) {
    const el = document.getElementById(id);
    if (el) el.remove();
  }
});
```

### Proposal

Add utilities to the `app/src/__utils__/` (inspired by the existing [api/src/test-utils](https://github.com/directus/directus/tree/main/api/src/test-utils) and use them in test files:

```ts
import { createGlobalMountConfig, setupTestOutlets, cleanupTestOutlets } from '@/__utils__/setup';

beforeEach(setupTestOutlets);
afterEach(cleanupTestOutlets);

mount(Component, { global: createGlobalMountConfig() });
```

### Benefits

- Less boilerplate per test file
- Single source of truth for test config

